{{!-- The Inventar tab: the three administrative lists.

This is deliberately *not* a second carry view. The Basics tab answers "what am
I wearing" and "what am I hauling" — questions asked mid-roll — and both are
derived views that show a piece only while it is in that state. This tab is the
ledger behind them: every object the character owns appears here exactly once,
whatever state it is in, which is what makes a piece that is neither worn nor
carried reachable at all. Creating, editing and deleting live here for the same
reason.

Features and Active Effects follow it because they are the other two things an
actor owns that are not objects — they cost no slots, so they can never appear
in the carry raster, and before this tab existed they had nowhere to be. --}}

{{!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------
Gear. One row per object, whatever roles it carries: the role buckets are
views onto this list, and listing them separately would show a piece once per
role it has. --}}
<div class='basics-section-header'>
  <h3 class='basics-section-title'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.CarrySlots'}}</h3>
  {{#if editable}}
    {{!-- `.section-add` is the look, `.inventory-add` is the action — the two
    are separate classes so the Merkmale button below can wear the same control
    without also triggering the gear-authoring dialog this one opens. --}}
    <a class='section-add inventory-add' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.AddHint"}}'>
      <i class='fas fa-plus'></i>
    </a>
  {{/if}}
</div>

{{#if inventory.length}}
  <ol class='items-list'>
    <li class='item flexrow items-header'>
      <div class='item-name'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.AddName'}}</div>
      <div class='item-roles'>{{localize 'TNO.Item.Roles'}}</div>
      <div class='item-prop'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Slots'}}</div>
      <div class='item-prop'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Quantity'}}</div>
      <div class='item-controls'></div>
    </li>

    {{#each inventory as |item|}}
      <li class='item flexrow draggable' data-item-id='{{item._id}}' draggable='true'>
        <div class='item-name'>
          {{!-- The role icon rather than the artwork, matching the carry grid:
          a repeated, recognisable glyph is quicker to scan down a list than
          ninety different portraits. --}}
          <div class='item-image'>
            <i class='fa-solid {{item.inventoryIcon}} inventory-item-icon' aria-hidden='true'></i>
          </div>
          <h4 title='{{item.name}}'>{{item.name}}</h4>
        </div>

        {{!-- What the piece *does*. An object with no role at all is the
        common case, so the column stays empty rather than carrying a
        "plain item" tag that would say nothing. --}}
        <div class='item-roles'>
          {{#each item.roleLabels as |label|}}
            <span class='item-role-tag'>{{localize label}}</span>
          {{/each}}
        </div>

        {{!-- Worn gear is exempt from the slot economy, so its cost reads as a
        dash rather than a zero: nothing is being spent, as opposed to a piece
        that genuinely costs nothing to carry. --}}
        <div class='item-prop'>
          {{#if item.isWorn}}—{{else}}{{item.slotCost}}{{/if}}
        </div>
        <div class='item-prop'>{{item.system.quantity}}</div>

        <div class='item-controls'>
          {{#if item.isWorn}}
            {{!-- A marker, not a control: taking a piece off belongs to the
            paper doll, which is the only view that knows which zones it
            occupies. --}}
            <span class='item-state' title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.WornHint"}}'>
              <i class='fas fa-shield-halved'></i>
            </span>
          {{/if}}
          <a class='item-control item-edit' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.Edit"}}'>
            <i class='fas fa-edit'></i>
          </a>
          {{!-- `@root.editable`, not `editable`: inside an `each` a bare name
          resolves against the item, which has no such key, so the whole block
          silently vanished. --}}
          {{#if @root.editable}}
            {{#unless item.isWorn}}
              <a class='item-control item-delete' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.Delete"}}'>
                <i class='fas fa-trash'></i>
              </a>
            {{else}}
              {{!-- Held back rather than hidden, so the row keeps its shape and
              says why: `system.equipment` addresses the piece by id, and
              deleting it out from under the doll would strand a zone. --}}
              <span class='item-control is-disabled' title='{{localize "TNO.Item.DeleteWornHint"}}'>
                <i class='fas fa-trash'></i>
              </span>
            {{/unless}}
          {{/if}}
        </div>
      </li>
    {{/each}}
  </ol>
{{else}}
  <p class='items-empty'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.Empty'}}</p>
{{/if}}

{{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-features.hbs"}}

{{!-- ------------------------------------------------------------------
Active Effects. Foundry's own mechanic rather than one of this system's, but
an effect applied to the character was previously visible nowhere on the
sheet at all. --}}
<div class='basics-section-header'>
  <h3 class='basics-section-title'>{{localize 'TNO.TabEffects'}}</h3>
</div>
{{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-effects.hbs"}}
